; cec_follower.loom
; An HDMI-CEC follower at logic level, on one open-drain wire: it receives
; every frame on the bus, checks the start bit's and every data bit's
; timing, keeps the frames sent to its logical address or broadcast,
; acknowledges each block of a frame sent to it by stretching the ACK bit
; to a 0, on time, and reports every kept frame, and every error, to OUTQ.
;
; Written on 2026-11-05, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035): CEC is in no design document.
; Hardware used: the M2 core only, plus the data memory of M3 slice B for
; the frame buffer: an open-drain BIDIR pin (OD_MASK, built for I2C), the
; timed waits with their timeout (WAITP ... T, built for I2C's clock
; stretching), NOW and TD, the tick restart on a TICK_INT write (built so
; a UART receiver can synchronise to its start bit), the FIFOs, LD and ST.
; No hardware knows CEC: the start bit's two windows, the sample point,
; the bit period limits, the blocks with EOM and ACK, the address filter
; and the ACK itself are firmware. It is weaker than a dedicated CEC
; controller in two ways: it measures each bit with three timed waits, so
; a glitch between them is not seen, and it does not answer a frame that
; follows its report too closely (below); see firmware/README.md.
;
; Pin: CEC = BIDIR1, open drain (OD_MASK bit 1). The program only pulls the
; line low or lets it go; the pull-up makes the high level. An initiator on
; the same chip (cec_initiator.loom, thread 0) has its own pin, BIDIR0, and
; the board wires the two into one bus.
;
; Sources: the figures and the windows of cec_initiator.loom's header
; (HDMI 1.3a Supplement 1, not read; the bit timings checked on 2026-11-06
; against the Linux kernel's drivers/media/cec/core/cec-pin.c, the rest
; unchecked). A follower's own rules:
;   sample      a data bit is the line 1.05 ms after its fall
;   ACK         for a block of a frame sent to its own address the follower
;               holds the ACK bit low for the 1.5 ms of a 0 from its fall;
;               for a broadcast it would hold it low to reject the frame,
;               which this follower never does
;   errors      the specification has a follower ignore a frame with a bit
;               outside its windows; this one reports it, as the Linux
;               kernel's cec-pin framework does
;
; Host words (INQ[1]). Once, before anything else:
;   word 1   this follower's logical address, bits 3:0 (0 to 14: 15 is the
;            broadcast address and no device's own)
; Report (OUTQ[1]), for every frame sent to it or broadcast, and for every
; frame that ended in an error before its header was complete:
;   status   4:0 the blocks received (header included, at most 16); 5
;            BCAST, the header's destination is 15; 6 DIRECT, it is this
;            follower's address (every block ACKed); 7 SHORT, a bit period
;            shorter than 2.05 ms; 8 LONG, a data bit still low 1.8 ms after
;            its fall (a 0 is at most 1.7 ms); 9 NOEOM, the line stayed
;            high for 2.85 ms inside a block, or after a block whose EOM
;            was 0 (the frame ended without its EOM); 10 OVERFLOW, more
;            than 16 blocks (the rest were followed and not kept); 15:11 0
;   data     ceil(blocks / 2) words, the header byte first in 15:8, the
;            next in 7:0 (an odd last byte in 15:8, 7:0 = 0)
; A frame for another follower is followed to its end and not reported.
; After SHORT or LONG it stops at that bit and waits for the line to idle.
; The report is pushed after the frame, and the PUSHes wait for room: a
; host that leaves OUTQ full holds the follower, which then misses frames.
; The next frame cannot start for 3 bit periods (7.2 ms, the shortest
; signal free time), which is the host's time to take a report of up to
; nine words.
;
; Timing, in ticks of 50 us (48 ticks a bit). Every fall restarts the tick
; grid (a TICK_INT write), so every time below is from the fall, late by
; the fall's detection, 2 to 6 clocks, plus two slots:
;   start bit   still low at 69 ticks (3.45 ms) and high by 79 (3.95 ms);
;               the next fall not before 85 (4.25 ms) and by 95 (4.75 ms).
;               The specification's windows are 3.5 to 3.9 and 4.3 to 4.7;
;               each is widened by one tick for the 50 us grid. A low that
;               fails is not a start bit and is ignored
;   data bit    sampled at 21 (1.05 ms); LONG if still low at 36 (1.8 ms);
;               SHORT if the next fall comes before 41 (2.05 ms); no next
;               fall by 57 (2.85 ms, the specification's 2.75 widened by two
;               ticks) is the end of the frame
;   ACK         the follower pulls the line low two slots after it sees the
;               ACK bit's fall (the initiator holds it low then for 0.6 ms
;               in any case) and lets go at 30 ticks (1.5 ms)
;
; Rate: as cec_initiator.loom, the host writes TICK_INT and TICK_FRAC
; before RUN, 50 us (2500 at 50 MHz); the RTL tests run 32 clocks a tick.
;
; Memory: 153 words: thread 1's quarter, 0x080 to 0x0FF, and 0x100 to
; 0x118 in thread 2's; the frame buffer, 16 words, at 0x1F0 to 0x1FF in thread 3's
; (one block a word, the byte in 7:0). Threads 2 and 3 must not run.
;
; Registers: r0 the own address, r1 the frame's flags (bit 0 BCAST, 1
; DIRECT, 2 SHORT, 3 LONG, 4 NOEOM, 5 OVERFLOW: the status bits 5 to 10),
; r2 the buffer pointer, r3 the bit counter and scratch, r4 the shifter,
; r5 the ACK state (0, 1 drive the next bit, 2 driving this one), r6 NOW
; at the last fall (TICK_INT while a fall is awaited), r7 scratch and
; rxt's result (0 a bit started, 4 SHORT, 8 LONG, 16 no next bit).

        .imem   512                     ; the macro build: quarters of 128 words
        .thread 1
        .tick   32                      ; the fastest tick proved
        .equ    CECPIN = 1              ; BIDIR1
        .pins   CEC = CECPIN
        .equ    CECBIT = 1 << CECPIN    ; its bit in OD_MASK
        .equ    BUF = 0x1F0             ; the frame, one block a word
        .equ    ST_MIN = 69             ; in ticks of 50 us from the fall
        .equ    ST_MAX = 79
        .equ    SP_MIN = 85
        .equ    SP_MAX = 95
        .equ    SAMPLE = 21
        .equ    LO0 = 30
        .equ    LONG = 36
        .equ    MINP = 41
        .equ    MAXP = 57
        .equ    F_BCAST = 1             ; r1, the frame's flags
        .equ    F_DIRECT = 2
        .equ    E_NOEOM = 16
        .equ    E_OVER = 32
        .equ    NONE = 16               ; rxt: no next bit

; OD_MASK first, read back three slots later (BUGS 14, dht22_host.loom).
start:  CSRR    r7, OD_MASK
        ORI     r7, CECBIT
        CSRW    OD_MASK, r7             ; CEC open drain
        NOP
        NOP
        CSRR    r7, OD_MASK
        ANDI    r7, CECBIT
        BZ      start                   ; lost to the other thread's write
        SETP    CEC, 1                  ; let go of the line
        LDI     r7, (1 << 5) | CECPIN
        CSRW    INGRP, r7               ; IN reads CEC into bit 0
        POP     r0                      ; the own logical address
        LDI     r5, 0

; Idle: a fall that may be a start bit.
idle:   WAITP   CEC, 1                  ; the line is high (unbounded)
        CSRR    r6, TICK_INT
        WAITP   CEC, 0                  ; a fall (unbounded)
        CSRW    TICK_INT, r6            ; the tick grid restarts at the fall
        SETD    0
        CSRR    r6, NOW                 ; F
        WAITD   ST_MIN
        JP      CEC, 1, idle            ; high already: too short
        SETD    ST_MAX - ST_MIN
        WAITP   CEC, 1, T
        BT      idle                    ; still low: too long
        MOV     r7, r6
        ADDI    r7, 63
        ADDI    r7, SP_MIN - 63
        CSRW    TD, r7
        WAITP   CEC, 0, T
        BNT     idle                    ; the next fall came too soon
        ADDI    r7, SP_MAX - SP_MIN
        CSRW    TD, r7
        CSRR    r6, TICK_INT
        WAITP   CEC, 0, T
        BT      idle                    ; no first bit: not a frame
        CSRW    TICK_INT, r6            ; the first data bit's fall
        SETD    0
        CSRR    r6, NOW

; A frame: blocks of 8 bits, EOM, ACK.
        LDI     r1, 0
        LDI     r5, 0                   ; no ACK pending from a broken frame
        MOV16   r2, BUF
block:  LDI     r3, 8
        LDI     r4, 0
dbit:   CALL    rxs
        CALL    rxt
        CMPI    r7, 0
        BNZ     err                     ; SHORT, LONG, or the frame stopped
        DJNZ    r3, dbit
        CALL    rxs                     ; EOM, the byte now in 8:1
        MOV16   r7, BUF
        CMP     r2, r7
        BNZ     ackdec                  ; not the header
        MOV     r7, r4
        SHRI    r7, 1
        ANDI    r7, 15                  ; the destination
        CMPI    r7, 15
        BNZ     h_own
        ORI     r1, F_BCAST
h_own:  CMP     r7, r0
        BNZ     ackdec
        ORI     r1, F_DIRECT
ackdec: MOV     r7, r1
        ANDI    r7, F_DIRECT
        BZ      ackbit                  ; not ours to acknowledge
        LDI     r5, 1                   ; drive the ACK bit at its fall
ackbit: CALL    rxt
        CMPI    r7, 0
        BNZ     err
        CALL    rxs                     ; the ACK bit, as the line shows it
        CALL    rxt                     ; r7: 0 the next block, NONE the end
        MOV     r3, r2
        SHRI    r3, 9                   ; the pointer has reached 0x200:
        BNZ     b_over                  ; 16 blocks kept already
        MOV     r3, r4
        SHRI    r3, 2                   ; the byte (r4 = byte, EOM, ACK)
        ST      r3, r2, 0
        ADDI    r2, 1
        JMP     b_next
b_over: ORI     r1, E_OVER
b_next: MOV     r3, r4
        ANDI    r3, 2
        BNZ     report                  ; EOM: the frame is complete
        CMPI    r7, 0
        BZ      block                   ; the next block has started
err:    OR      r1, r1, r7              ; SHORT, LONG, or NONE = NOEOM

; The report: kept when the header is incomplete, or addressed here or to all.
report: MOV16   r7, BUF
        SUB     r3, r2, r7              ; the blocks kept
        BZ      r_go
        MOV     r7, r1
        ANDI    r7, F_BCAST | F_DIRECT
        BZ      idle                    ; another follower's frame
r_go:   MOV     r7, r1
        SHLI    r7, 5
        OR      r7, r7, r3
        PUSH    r7                      ; the status
        MOV16   r2, BUF
r_word: CMPI    r3, 0
        BZ      idle
        LD      r7, r2, 0
        SWAP    r7, r7                  ; the first byte in 15:8
        ADDI    r2, 1
        DEC     r3
        BZ      r_push
        LD      r4, r2, 0
        OR      r7, r7, r4              ; the second in 7:0
        ADDI    r2, 1
        DEC     r3
r_push: PUSH    r7
        JMP     r_word

; rxs: the sample. TD is the bit's fall F; waits to F + 1.05 ms and shifts
; the line into r4 bit 0.
rxs:    WAITD   SAMPLE
        IN      r7
        SHLI    r4, 1
        OR      r4, r4, r7
        RET

; rxt: the rest of the bit and the next fall. Releases the ACK at 1.5 ms if
; it drives this bit, checks the bit is high by LONG and that no fall comes
; before MINP, then waits for the next fall until MAXP. At the fall it
; restarts the tick grid, drives the ACK low if asked (r5 = 1), sets TD and
; r6 to the fall and returns r7 = 0; otherwise r7 = 4 (SHORT), 8 (LONG) or
; NONE.
rxt:    CMPI    r5, 2
        BNZ     rxt_h
        WAITD   LO0 - SAMPLE            ; 1.5 ms after the fall
        SETP    CEC, 1                  ; the ACK's 0 ends
        LDI     r5, 0
rxt_h:  MOV     r7, r6
        ADDI    r7, LONG
        CSRW    TD, r7
        WAITP   CEC, 1, T
        BT      rxt_lo                  ; still low at 1.8 ms
        ADDI    r7, MINP - LONG
        CSRW    TD, r7
        WAITP   CEC, 0, T
        BNT     rxt_sh                  ; a fall before 2.05 ms
        ADDI    r7, MAXP - MINP
        CSRW    TD, r7
        CSRR    r6, TICK_INT
        WAITP   CEC, 0, T
        BT      rxt_no                  ; no next bit by 2.85 ms
        CSRW    TICK_INT, r6            ; the tick grid restarts at the fall
        CMPI    r5, 1
        BNZ     rxt_s
        SETP    CEC, 0                  ; the ACK: hold the bit low
        LDI     r5, 2
rxt_s:  SETD    0
        CSRR    r6, NOW
        LDI     r7, 0
        RET
rxt_lo: LDI     r7, 8
        JMP     rxt_e
rxt_sh: LDI     r7, 4
        JMP     rxt_e
rxt_no: LDI     r7, NONE
rxt_e:  SETD    0                       ; an anchor on the way out: the
        RET                             ; caller stops at r7 != 0, which
                                        ; the deadline checker cannot see
